From 9b6ed3230fe629d5860e383cb279c1230d7c6ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BOAR R&D <noreply>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:37:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] routing: turn the per-answer health caution on by default

The health caution (a notice above a model-written, health-shaped answer, in three tiers by grounding: no-source, beyond-source, sourced) was an opt-in engine option. The app ships with a safety warning, so it is now on unless a caller sets deps.warn to false. With it off, every event, text and receipt code is exactly as before. The banner strings are unchanged.

The caution replaces the weak_sources warning and the uncited preface only when the client says it renders the caution (new deps.warnRendered, default false). Without a renderer, warn events and the warn:<tier> code are still sent, but the old notices stay exactly as before, so a client that cannot show the caution (the Android chat today) never loses its only notice. A client that renders the warn event sets warnRendered to true. The warn event and done.warn carry that as `rendered`, and the reducer clears weakSources only when rendered is not false.

Tests: the existing on/off cases now set the flag explicitly, and a new case checks that an unset deps.warn means on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply>
